  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the lifetime of a fuse. Then we have $X\u223cN(\\mu ,1\\,{500}^{2}),$  and we want to find the mean $\\mu .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X<7\\,000)=0.25.$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<7\\,000) & =0.25 \\\\ P(Z<\\frac{7\\,000-\\mu }{1\\,500}) & =0.25 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{7\\,000-\\mu }{1\\,500}) & =0.25 \\\\ \\frac{7\\,000-\\mu }{1\\,500} & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.25)\u2248-0.6745.\n$$\n\nFinally then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7\\,000-\\mu }{1\\,500} & =-0.6745 \\\\ 7\\,000-\\mu  & =-1011.75 \\\\ \\mu  & \u22488012\\,\\text{hours}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
